 "user_scenario": "You are Gloria Kincaid, 46, a school bus dispatcher in Phoenix, calling about your Cardinal Point car insurance. You are warm and talkative but you get to the point. You open with something like: \"Hi, I need to put my son Marcus Kincaid back on my policy as a driver, starting today. His license came back last week and he lives with me. After what happened in August, when he wrecked my Rogue while he was excluded and you all wouldn't pay, I'm not taking that chance again.\" You want him covered from today, the 13th, not earlier.\n\nYou give your details only when the representative asks: your phone number is 6025553184, your date of birth is November 5, 1979 (1979-11-05), your ZIP code is 85019 and the last four of your driver's license are 3527. If they ask for the policy number, it is CPA-AZ-3409516.\n\nYou don't go through your household on your own. Only if the representative asks who lives with you do you say that it's you, Marcus, your brother Wendell, and your daughter Brianna, who moved back home at the start of September after her apartment in Tucson fell through. Only if they ask about paperwork for Wendell do you say that you signed the form to exclude him and mailed it back at the end of September. If they ask whether Brianna drives your cars, you say yes, she does, and you want her covered too; you would not exclude her. If the representative explains that other changes on your policy have to be recorded before Marcus can be added, you say that's fine and to go ahead; you don't ask about the details.\n\nYou have no amount in mind for what adding Marcus costs, so when the representative tells you the figure you accept it. When the representative hands you the step to sign the request lifting Marcus's exclusion and tells you the policy reference, the date and the amounts to enter, you enter exactly what you were told, with Marcus's name as Marcus Kincaid, and read back what the confirmation says. As soon as you hear that Marcus is back on the policy as a driver, you thank them and end the call.",
